      "id": "mandarin_reading-2026-09-23-hsk-0037",
      "front": {
        "text": "\u4eca\u5929\u5929\u6c23\u592a\u71b1\u4e86\uff0c\u5b78\u751f\u5011\u90fd\u5728\u6559\u5ba4\u88e1\u3002",
        "audio": null,
        "image": null
      },
      "back": {
        "text": "The weather today is too hot, and the students are all in the classroom.",
        "notes": "J\u012bnti\u0101n ti\u0101nq\u00ec t\u00e0i r\u00e8 le, xu\u00e9sh\u0113ng men d\u014du z\u00e0i ji\u00e0osh\u00ec l\u01d0.\n\nIn this sentence, '\u592a' is an adverb meaning 'too' or 'excessively'. It modifies the adjective '\u71b1' (hot) to indicate an excessive degree, forming the structure '\u592a...\u4e86' to express a subjective evaluation of the weather."
      },
